{
  "id": 461951713,
  "iid": 23806,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "TECMP: Fix integer overflow (OSS Fuzz issue 468513074)",
  "description": "When subtracting two timestamps expressed as 64-bit unsigned\nintegers of nanoseconds past the Unix epoch, and storing the\nresult in a 64-bit signed integer, in the extremely unlikely\neven that one of the timestamps is past 2262-04-12 (which\nmust be the second one here, as the first one is a 62-bit\nunsigned integer in the packet), it can overflow. That's\nextremely unlikely, and the time for the time delta is hidden\nanyway, so just suppress the overflow warning.\n\nOSS Fuzz Issue 468513074\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
